# F0 resumption acceptance report

Operational observations now support closure of F0 within the explicitly adopted
local foundation boundary, subject to the final recorded integrity/governance
checks. The current criterion matrix is matrix.json; raw checks and numerical
samples are in observation-checks.json and each named run directory. This record
supersedes the open graphical/performance findings in f0-execution-20261102 only
for the new observations. Earlier failures and their original identities remain.

| Former blocker | Current evidence and disposition |
| --- | --- |
| Native Wayland journey lacked workspace correlation | Identified primary-session run: workspace, exact artifacts, APPROVED/REJECTED history, native keyboard events, child disappearance and natural exit 0; original-binary isolated flow and six support cells corroborate it |
| Shift+Tab and unstable graphical observation | XTEST modifier failure reproduced; compositor input delivers Shift, reverse focus and activation. Native first-input readiness corrected. 36 X11 tests across six cells, three native held-verification runs and three coverage-instrumented X11 held runs pass |
| GUI/frame/CPU budgets and support matrix were proposals | Maintainer explicitly adopted decision-proposal.md; twelve separate metric cells satisfy the adopted limits, with backend/session and observer boundaries retained |

| Metric | Maximum observed across 12 cells | Adopted limit |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Input to observed GUI pixels | 95.30 ms | 120 ms |
| Client draw through presentation-call return | 82.21 ms | 125 ms |
| GUI RSS | 49.37 MiB | 64 MiB |
| Idle CPU, each 10-second window | 0 measured ticks | <=5% of one core |

Every cell has three warmups and twenty measured response samples; the client
instrumentation captures the corresponding draw/present calls. Each cell has three
10-second idle observations. CPU uses process ticks at 100 Hz: zero delta is below
the measurement resolution, not a claim of zero work. Wayland RSS is sampled at
20 ms; X11 records the kernel lifetime high-water mark, a conservative upper bound
for that cell. The independent large-history budget remains unchanged.

Scope: Linux x86_64 on the identified host; X11 and native Wayland; scales
100/150/200%; logical content sizes 640x480 and 900x700. Native matrix measurements
use isolated headless Mutter with compositor capture; X11 uses Xwayland within that
isolated environment and client framebuffer capture. The primary Wayland desktop
journey is separately identified. Neither method measures physical scanout, and
neither grants universal compositor/GPU support, assistive-technology conformance,
a sandbox, durable storage or later roadmap capabilities.

Changes are bounded to reproducible observation harnesses, SDD/decision/evidence
records and one governance-export exclusion for this operational evidence directory.
The new export regression fails before the exclusion and passes afterward. No
application source, product dependency or lockfile changed. The initial 220 bindings
matched; unchanged backend, security, coverage, domain and extension observations
are retained by identity and scope, not claimed as newly executed.

See graphical-review.md for competing explanations, failed probes, successful
repetitions and limitations. Current P01/P05/Q05–Q08/Q13 and AC-05 require the
new evidence and final integrity checks; other clauses retain their independently
supported scope. Persistence remains a separate authorized-decision track before
F3/MVP. No commits, publication, global installation or new roadmap execution.
